    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0527" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/593</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Netherland Minister of Foreign Affairs to the
                        Netherland Minister at Washington</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Van
                        Rappard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<hi rendition="#italic">Left at the
                            Department of State by the Netherland Minister</hi>, <lb/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 4, 1915</hi>.</date>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British and French Ministers, joined orally by Russian Minister, declared by note
                    of December 26<anchor n="1" xml:id="d393-f1"/> contraband merchandise consigned
                    to recently constituted Netherlands Oversea Trust not to be stopped. They also
                    declared will not stop foodstuffs which are not necessaries of life consigned to
                    merchants unless these merchants are beyond doubt intermediaries for delivery to
                    enemy governments.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
